  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s25/c245c2ea> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/integrate/65593144> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s25/c245c2ea> ;
  triage:notes """Full ordered sweep of crates/atm/src/composition.rs across all 9 supplied worktrees (feature/pAG-s18 through integrate/phase-AG) found zero occurrences of the terms 'loopback' or 'self poison'/'self_poison' anywhere in the file on any branch -- no test, no comment, no cross-reference pointer note. The pattern is fully repeatable and unchanged since AG.19 introduced it: every downstream sprint branch inherited the same silent absence with no intervening fix. Equivalent-substance coverage was independently confirmed present on all checked branches: crates/atm-core/tests/mailbox_locking.rs:843 retains a 'historical self poison' test case, and crates/atm-daemon/src/tests/runtime_root/self_ip.rs contains multiple loopback/self-ip discovery and configuration tests (e.g. discover_non_loopback_ipv4_for_test, configure_secure_loopback). This confirms 'tests may relocate, never be deleted' is satisfied in substance; the open gap is purely the missing pointer note in composition.rs and the sprint doc's literal (unfulfilled) in-place-update instruction. highest_open_branch by raw sweep order is integrate/phase-AG (order index 9), but per project convention fix dispatch never targets integrate directly, and the caller has confirmed integrate/phase-AG's current tip has not yet merge-forwarded AG.19's changes -- it sits outside the AG.19-AG.25 feature-branch merge-forward chain at time of this triage. promote_to_branch is therefore set to feature/pAG-s25-live-two-daemon-proof, the highest-order branch inside that chain; the fix will reach integrate/phase-AG via the normal sequential merge-forward once dispatched and merged there.""" .

